.TH FINANCE-MAIL-POST 1 "2026-11-11" "Finance Infrastructure" "Nexus Host Utilities"
.SH NAME
finance-mail-post \- post future, authenticated CIBC credit alerts as provisional Wealthfolio withdrawals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/data/bin/finance-mail-post
.RB [ --preview | --apply ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Only the historically verified CIBC credit-card sender, subject, body, one
card label and suffix may route to the protected Wealthfolio account mapping.
The route lives in root-only
.B /etc/nexus/secrets/finance-mail-route.json
and was activated after 391 unique merchant/amount/date historical matches to
the same CIBC credit account and none to the two other CIBC accounts. This is
an evidence-based account inference, not an independently supplied card/account
number. If account name, suffix, template, trusted Proton authentication-results
or staged evidence changes, stop rather than guessing. No pre-activation
messages are imported. Debit-card, other-bank and unknown-card templates are
not supported.
.PP
The default
.B --preview
is read-only. With
.B --apply
it first checks the CIBC message against the staged authenticated alert and
Proton Bridge mail, then searches the target account for an existing withdrawal
with exact CAD cents, a near date and strongly matching merchant. A unique
existing transaction is not re-posted; ambiguous or oversized purchases require
review. New notifications are posted as
.B provisional
WITHDRAWAL activities with merchant and a deterministic source-key marker.
The mail timestamp may precede settlement and is not a verified posting date.
The statement importer must reconcile these records before adding the later
bank ledger row; no automatic category or confirmed receipt link is inferred.
.PP
Each new source key receives a protected, fsynced pre-commit journal before
Wealthfolio write, followed by saved activity-ID readback and a verified journal
state. Uncertain commits are never blindly retried. One narrowly scoped
accounts/activities temporary write token is issued only when needed and is
revoked with readback; it expires after two hours if interrupted. The
.B finance-intake.service
runs receipt projection, mail evidence staging and receipt matching before this
poster. A newly posted activity can therefore be considered by the matcher on
the next hourly run, subject to exact amount, date, merchant and uniqueness.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Host Python 3.9+, Docker and PostgreSQL client, systemd-creds, bws,
Bitwarden-held Proton Bridge/Wealthfolio credentials, localhost IMAP 1143,
finance-mail-ingest, /usr/local/sbin/receipt-match-audit, a healthy Wealthfolio
3.12.0 native MCP/API and finance-analytics PostgreSQL. Run as root. Protect
.B /var/lib/finance-mail-post
(mode 0700, journals 0600), the 0600 route and an up-to-date encrypted
Wealthfolio database recovery point. This is not a substitute for off-host
and whole-appdata recovery.
.SH OUTPUT
Aggregate counts only; no message, merchant, account ID, card suffix or
credential is printed. A nonzero exit leaves a protected journal for manual
inspection and does not delete or overwrite existing Wealthfolio activities.
.SH ROLLBACK
Disable the poster's ExecStart in the Git-managed unit and guarded-deploy the
change. For a journal stage
.B posted,
verify the exact saved Wealthfolio ID and dependent receipt candidate links,
then delete only the reviewed provisional activity via the app's supported
interface. Do not delete an activity classified as pre-existing. For
.B precommit
or
.B committed_unverified,
search the exact source marker first; a commit may have succeeded even if the
process failed. Do not rerun the posting blindly. The older database-only GPG
snapshot is a last-resort recovery aid, not permission to overwrite later owner
transactions. The private
.B iragonforce/ops
repository owns the program, timer unit and manual.
